commands/EXTVERSION                                       commands/EXTVERSION

   NAME
	EXTVERSION - Find the extra version number.

   FORMAT
	EXTVERSION [<library|script|file>] [VSTRING|HELP]

   TEMPLATE
	NAME,VSTRING/S,HELP/S

   PATH
	C:EXTVERSION

   FUNCTION
	EXTVERSION finds the extra version number of a library,	command,
	script or simply any file if the extra version string has been
	correctly set in the file.

	EXTVERSION with no <library|file> argument prints the XXXX
	XXXXXX<<TODO: text>>.

	The VSTRING keyword requires a NAME parameter that is not a wildcard
	pattern. If version information can be found for the named file,
	it will be printed in the standard format; if no such information
	is available, an empty line will be printed instead. This feature
	is useful for script files.

	The HELP keyword will print some information regarding the
	EXTVERSION command syntax among other things.

   EXAMPLES
	    1> EXTVERSION
	    Kickstart version 36.202 Workbench version 36.77

	    1> EXTVERSION Prefs/Font
	    Prefs/Font version 36.191

	    1> EXTVERSION C:Version VSTRING
	    $VER: Extversion 51.13 (20.8.2005)

   SEE ALSO
	VERSION
